# >>> agent-harness managed >>>
# Shared content, COPIED into each consuming repo by the harness — git will not read an
# ignore file through a symlink. Edit it in the harness, not in a consuming repo: the
# harness rewrites everything between its managed markers every run, and anything edited
# there is lost. Lines outside the markers are left alone.
#
# READ scripts/README.md IN THE HARNESS -> "The two copied files" BEFORE DELETING A LINE.
# Some entries below look redundant and are not, and `.claude/settings.local.json` is
# deliberately absent rather than overlooked. Patterns a repo adds for itself go outside
# the managed markers.

# A safety net for the old layout, not duplication — read the README.
active-work-context/*
sessions/
*-status.log
*-status.log.*
*hook-payloads/

logging-config.json

agent-status.log
agent-state*.json
agent-state.json.lock
responses/

# These land inside the harness checkout, where one untracked file freezes updates for
# every repo on the machine. Read the README before dropping either.
hooks/log.jsonl
hooks/state/

# Resolves to the CONSUMER's .claude/local/, not this checkout — read the README.
local/

input/*
!input/README.md
scheduled_tasks.lock
# <<< agent-harness managed <<<
